{"id": 26, "ts": 1780621623.3950896, "event": "public_discussion_message", "round": 2, "agent": "sarah_mitchell", "message": "I remain convinced that **Candidate\u202fC** is the best overall fit. While Candidate\u202fA shows impressive foresight (\u201canticipates dangerous situations\u201d), excellent spatial vision and strong leadership, we have no concrete evidence of his operational reliability or crew\u2011cooperation, and his difficulty accepting criticism and being unorganized raise serious doubts about adaptability and consistency. Candidate\u202fB\u2019s \u201cvery conscientious\u201d attitude and stress resilience are offset by the \u201cgrumpy\u201d and \u201cuncooperative\u201d descriptors that directly threaten the crew\u2011cooperation essential for long\u2011haul flights. Candidate\u202fD excels in concentration, problem\u2011solving and takes responsibility seriously, yet his \u201carrogant\u201d demeanor, \u201cweak leadership\u201d and lack of observed teamwork make him a risk in the cockpit environment. In contrast, Candidate\u202fC consistently demonstrates quick, correct decision\u2011making, calmness under pressure, 100\u202f% reliability and a positive crew atmosphere\u2014core safety\u2011critical criteria\u2014while his communication and egocentric tendencies can be mitigated through CRM training. Therefore I continue to vote for **Candidate\u202fC**."}
